<section class="lp-section lp-caps lp-reveal">
    <div class="lp-container">
        <div class="lp-caps-head">
            <div>
                <p class="lp-eyebrow">The Workshop</p>
                <h2 class="lp-h2">What it <em>can draw on</em>.</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="lp-lede" style="padding-bottom: 10px">
                What the standard way does for everyone, and what the workshop adds for teams
                that administrators set up.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="caps-grid">
            <div class="cap">
                <div class="ico"><LandingIllustrations Name="CapSources" /></div>
                <div class="meta">— Your files</div>
                <h3>Your files, <em>in full</em></h3>
                <p>The writer gets your PDF, Word and text files completely, up to a size limit. Workshop teams can also use a knowledge base, papers and the web.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="cap">
                <div class="ico"><LandingIllustrations Name="CapFilter" /></div>
                <div class="meta">— Questions</div>
                <h3>It <em>asks first</em></h3>
                <p>If something important is missing, you get a few short questions with answers to click before it starts. You can skip them.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="cap">
                <div class="ico"><LandingIllustrations Name="CapModels" /></div>
                <div class="meta">— Models</div>
                <h3>A model <em>for each role</em></h3>
                <p>Each part of the work uses a model chosen for its role. Administrators can add providers in the workshop.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="cap">
                <div class="ico"><LandingIllustrations Name="CapExport" /></div>
                <div class="meta">— Finishing</div>
                <h3>Ready <em>to download</em></h3>
                <p>Download every text as Word, PDF or Markdown. Workshop teams can add finishing steps such as a summary.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="cap">
                <div class="ico"><LandingIllustrations Name="CapLearn" /></div>
                <div class="meta">— Honesty</div>
                <h3>It says <em>what it checked</em></h3>
                <p>Every text written the standard way comes with what was checked, what is still open and what was assumed. It never claims to be flawless.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="cap">
                <div class="ico"><LandingIllustrations Name="CapTrust" /></div>
                <div class="meta">— Trust</div>
                <h3>Built for <em>trust</em></h3>
                <p>Accounts per person, self-hosted and open source. Keys for outside services come from the server's settings, not from forms.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
